{
  "dom_id": "step-q97024",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/ffbfa9e7aa3462d7f60e8d70a00e0a5c1f1044bd270911259a6a1f1ce6d5b30b.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,1)$, $(0,0),$ $(-2,2).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/c26cdc9a92481b7e2a7f9e128656d42c093b5fbb8d2ca4d02dc3bb262ce64341.png)",
